\begin{lem}
There is no ``universal computable relation.'' That is, there is no
binary computable relation $R(x,y)$, with the following property:
whenever $S(y)$ is a unary computable relation, there is some $k$ such
that for every $y$, $S(y)$ is true if and only if $R(k,y)$ is true.
\end{lem}

target.raw_text:
\begin{lem}
Ora ana ``relasi komputabel universal''. Tegese, ora ana relasi
komputabel biner $R(x,y)$ kang nduweni sipat mangkene:
kapan wae $S(y)$ iku relasi komputabel uner, ana sawijining $k$ saengga
kanggo saben $y$, $S(y)$ bener yen lan mung yen $R(k,y)$ bener.
\end{lem}

