\begin{proof}
Suppose $C$ is a computable set such that $\Th{Q} \subseteq C$ and
$\Th{\bar Q} \subseteq \Complement{C}$. Let $R(x,y)$ be the relation
\begin{quote}
$x$ codes a formula $!D(u)$ and $!D(\num y)$ is in $C$.
\end{quote}
We will show that $R(x,y)$ is a universal computable relation, yielding
a contradiction.

target.raw_text:
\begin{proof}
Upamana $C$ himpunan komputabel saengga $\Th{Q} \subseteq C$ lan
$\Th{\bar Q} \subseteq \Complement{C}$. Upamana $R(x,y)$ iku relasi
\begin{quote}
$x$ ngodeake formula $!D(u)$ kang variabel bebas mung bisa u lan $!D(\num y)$ kalebu ing $C$.
\end{quote}
Kita bakal nuduhake yen $R(x,y)$ iku relasi komputabel universal, kang
nuwuhake kontradiksi.

source.raw_text:
Suppose $S(y)$ is computable, represented by $!D_S(u)$ in $\Th{Q}$. Then
\begin{eqnarray*}
S(\num n) & \lif & \Th{Q} \Proves !D_S(\num n) \\
& \lif & !D_S(\num n) \in C
\end{eqnarray*}
and 
\begin{eqnarray*}
\lnot S(\num n) & \lif & \Th{Q} \Proves \lnot !D_S(\num n) \\
& \lif & !D_S(\num n) \in \Th{\bar Q} \\
& \lif & !D_S(\num n) \not\in C
\end{eqnarray*}
So $S(y)$ is equivalent to $R(\#(!D_S(\num u)),y)$. 
\end{proof}

target.raw_text:
Upamana $S(y)$ komputabel, diwakili dening $!D_S(u)$ ing
$\Th{Q}$. Mula
\begin{eqnarray*}
S(n) & \lif & \Th{Q} \Proves !D_S(\num n) \\
& \lif & !D_S(\num n) \in C
\end{eqnarray*}
lan
\begin{eqnarray*}
\lnot S(n) & \lif & \Th{Q} \Proves \lnot !D_S(\num n) \\
& \lif & !D_S(\num n) \in \Th{\bar Q} \\
& \lif & !D_S(\num n) \not\in C
\end{eqnarray*}
Mula $S(y)$ ekuivalen karo $R(\Gn{!D_S(u)},y)$. Cathetan koreksi sumber OLPL-794: argumen meta S saiki wilangan n, lan parameter R saiki kode formula D-S kanthi variabel u. Numeral n ing formula substitusi tetep dijaga.
\end{proof}

source.raw_text:
\begin{thm}
Let $\Th{T}$ be any theory in the language of arithmetic that is
consistent with $\Th{Q}$ (i.e., $\Th{T} \cup \Th{Q}$ is
consistent). Then $\Th{T}$ is undecidable.
\end{thm}

target.raw_text:
\begin{thm}
Upamana $\Th{T}$ teori sembarang ing basa aritmetika kang konsisten
karo $\Th{Q}$ (yaiku, $\Th{T} \cup \Th{Q}$ konsisten). Mula
$\Th{T}$ ora bisa diputusake.
\end{thm}

source.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
  First-order logic for the language of arithmetic (that is, the set
  $\Setabs{!A}{\text{$!A$ is provable in first-order logic}}$) is
  undecidable.
\end{cor}

target.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
  Logika tataran kapisan kanggo basa aritmetika (yaiku, himpunan
  $\Setabs{!A}{\text{$!A$ bisa dibuktekake ing logika tataran kapisan}}$)
  ora bisa diputusake.
\end{cor}

source.raw_text:
\begin{proof}
First-order logic is the set of consequences of $\emptyset$,
which is consistent with~$\Th{Q}$.
\end{proof}

target.raw_text:
\begin{proof}
Logika tataran kapisan iku himpunan akibat saka $\emptyset$,
kang konsisten karo~$\Th{Q}$.
\end{proof}

source.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
There is no decidable extension of $\Th{ZFC}$.
\end{cor}

target.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
Ora ana ekstensi konsisten saka $\Th{ZFC}$ kang bisa diputusake.
\end{cor}
Cathetan koreksi sumber OLPL-795: simpulan saiki kanthi eksplisit mbutuhake konsistensi. Ekstensi ora konsisten mbuktekake kabeh ukara lan bisa diputusake, mula ora kalebu simpulan iki.

source.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
There is no complete, consistent, computably !!{axiomatizable} extension of
$\Th{ZFC}$. 
\end{cor}

target.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
Ora ana ekstensi $\Th{ZFC}$ kang jangkep, konsisten, lan
!!{axiomatizable} kanthi komputabel.
\end{cor}

source.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
First-order logic for any language with a binary relation symbol is
undecidable.
\end{cor}

target.raw_text:
\begin{cor}
Logika tataran kapisan kanggo saben basa kang nduweni simbol relasi biner
ora bisa diputusake.
\end{cor}
